.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt LS 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ls
.Nd list visible directory entries and native metadata
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l
.Op Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
List the working directory when no path is supplied.
For a directory, print sorted entry names, one per line, with a trailing
slash on directories.
A file operand prints that operand's path.
With multiple operands, directory listings have a
.Ql path:
header.
There is no hidden-name filter, terminal column layout, recursive listing,
colour or Unix permission display.
.Pp
.Fl l
adds kind
.Pq Ql d No or Ql - ,
read-only flag
.Pq Ql ro No or Ql -- ,
link count, byte size, and modification time in UTC to the minute.
Unknown modification time is printed as
.Ql - .
The size column is aligned within each listing.
ABSD has no owner, group or mode bits.
The object's read-only flag alone does not describe this session's mount
access; consult
.Xr stat 1
or
.Xr df 1 .
Options precede operands; a later option word is a path.
.Ql --
ends option processing; use it or a
.Ql ./
prefix for a name beginning with a dash.
Unknown leading options return status 2.
.Pp
The listing is limited to this process's visible filesystem view.
No file is changed.
A failed operand is diagnosed on standard error and later operands are
attempted.
Output failure stops listing; broken pipe is quiet.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 for successful listing; 1 for a path, metadata or output failure;
2 for an unknown leading option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ls -l /home/operator
ls -- /etc/network.conf
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr df 1 ,
.Xr stat 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
